review_comments:
I find that the @@character_set_client is not considered when the column is binary(`blob`) type.

MySQL:
```sql
drop table if exists t;
create table t(a blob(100));
set character_set_connection = 'gbk';
set character_set_client = 'gbk';
set character_set_results = 'gbk';
insert into t values ("你好");
select hex(a) from t;
```
```
+--------------+
| hex(a)       |
+--------------+
| E4BDA0E5A5BD |
+--------------+
```

Try this:
```mysql
drop table if exists t;
create table t(a blob(100));
set character_set_client = 'gbk';
insert into t values ("你好");
select hex(a) from t;
```

MySQL will ignore the transform when `connection` and `client` are `gbk` which not same as TiDB does.

Seems you updated your PR to solve blob problem, but it's not only for `blob`, try this:
```mysql
create table t (b blob, d json);
insert into t values ('你好', '{"测试": "你好"}');
select * from t;
```

And my question is why we need `dataIsBinary` here?

@Defined2014 The difference can be unexpected:

If we change it to 0x81, `一二三` is decoded to `涓€浜屼笁` instead of `涓?簩涓?`. The latter is compatible with MySQL.

https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/b4df7ca4dcc4a851a1a04d4348dee2b153618a7b/parser/charset/encoding_test.go#L45-L58

Because I am trying to make it compatible with MySQL:

```sql
set @@sql_mode = '';
drop table if exists t;
create table t (a char(10) charset ascii);
insert into t values ('😊');
select * from t;
```

```
mysql> select * from t;
+------+
| a    |
+------+
| ?    |
+------+
1 row in set (0.00 sec)
```

Note there is only one `?`.
